{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/lemma_argument_impure_1.march","start_line":7,"start_col":28,"end_line":7,"end_col":38,"message":"Function `cat` is structurally recursive but not tail-recursive. If the recursive call is the direct argument of a constructor in tail position, tail-recursion-modulo-cons compiles it to a loop with no extra stack (it always runs). Otherwise it uses O(depth) stack space and deep input can overflow the stack — consider an accumulator parameter.","code":"non_tail_recursion","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"RECURSION"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/lemma_argument_impure_1.march","start_line":25,"start_col":4,"end_line":25,"end_col":25,"message":"the argument of this call of the lemma `cat_nil` is not a pure term: lemma calls are removed before the program runs, so erasing it would also erase `noisy_list`. Bind it to a name first.","code":"lemma_argument_impure","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"REFINEMENT"}
